WEBVTT

00:02.100 --> 00:05.645
"It seems today that all you see

00:05.645 --> 00:09.066
"Is violence in movies and sex on TV

00:09.191 --> 00:12.945
"But where are those
good old-fashioned values

00:12.945 --> 00:15.031
"On which we used to rely?

00:15.740 --> 00:19.077
"Lucky there's a family guy

00:19.202 --> 00:24.207
"Lucky there's a man who positively
can do all the things that make us

00:24.292 --> 00:25.668
"Laugh and cry

00:25.751 --> 00:31.299
"He's a family guy

00:33.802 --> 00:38.682
- So, tell me about yourself, Tina.
- I really love music.

00:38.807 --> 00:44.647
Me, too. I just saw Don Giovanni. In my
opinion, the best opera of the 18th century.

00:44.730 --> 00:48.485
- Definitely.
- And the use of recitative throughout...

00:48.611 --> 00:51.946
- Mozart was a genius.
- Oh, yeah, re... cita... tive...

00:52.030 --> 00:54.324
is really, you know, where it's at.

00:54.448 --> 00:57.452
- Sir, are we ready to order?
- Whoa. Hold on a second.

00:57.577 --> 01:01.748
- You don't know what I'm talking about.
- Sure I do. Opera's bitchin'!

01:01.833 --> 01:07.673
OK. I guess I'll have the escar-got
and a glass of chab-lis.

01:07.798 --> 01:10.384
Same here. Escar-got and the chab-lis.

01:13.095 --> 01:15.723
Don't dawdle, Jonas. Play your exercises.

01:15.807 --> 01:18.227
Brian, what happened with your date?

01:18.310 --> 01:21.854
- Same as always. She was an idiot.
- Oh, Brian.

01:21.981 --> 01:24.064
Don't slow down, Jonas. Keep the rhythm.

01:24.148 --> 01:29.489
"Bum, bum, bum, bum
Brian, your standards are ridiculously high

01:29.489 --> 01:34.784
"You'll never find a girl unless
you compromise so you can find your love

01:34.910 --> 01:37.287
"I don't think
I have to compromise a thing

01:37.412 --> 01:39.999
"I'd rather be alone
if someone doesn't get me

01:40.124 --> 01:42.627
"How long has the coffee
been on the burner?

01:42.627 --> 01:45.338
"I could really use a cup about now

01:45.422 --> 01:48.049
"Oh, it's not very fresh
I meant to make more

01:48.133 --> 01:52.096
"I made the mistake of watching Oprah
She had on James Garner

01:52.221 --> 01:56.059
- " James Garner? What's he plugging?
- " Some crappy movie on TNT

01:56.184 --> 01:58.478
Very good, Jonas. I'll see you next week.

01:58.478 --> 02:01.482
So, you don't think
these women understand you?

02:01.606 --> 02:05.360
I'm not comfortable
talking about this a-melodically.

02:05.443 --> 02:08.698
- Peter, could you...
- Hang on a second.

02:08.698 --> 02:12.452
Now back to "The Life and Times
of Grizzly Adams".

02:13.495 --> 02:17.458
- Grizzly? Who's Steve?
- What?

02:17.541 --> 02:20.585
There's a message
on the machine from Steve.

02:20.585 --> 02:26.217
Oh, yeah, Steve. He's... new to the mountain.
I met him down at the general store.

02:26.302 --> 02:30.055
- He makes canoes.
- Oh.

02:30.178 --> 02:34.225
- How come I've never met him?
- He hasn't really been here that long.

02:34.351 --> 02:37.979
- Long enough to get your number!
- Ben! Ben!

02:38.104 --> 02:39.648
Dammit.

02:39.775 --> 02:43.821
Look at that Grizzly Adams.
Look at how confident he is, how majestic.

02:43.945 --> 02:47.157
- I'm gonna grow a beard.
- Peter, you know I hate beards.

02:47.282 --> 02:51.036
Oh, no, it's time I joined the ranks
of great men with beards.

02:51.120 --> 02:56.458
Why do you think Jesus Christ was
so popular? Because of all the magic tricks?

02:56.458 --> 03:01.131
Brian's depressed. Could you take him
with you to the laser rock show tonight?

03:01.256 --> 03:04.593
Sure. That's one thing I'm good at -
cheering people up.

03:05.636 --> 03:09.806
Mr and Mrs Ramsey,
JonBenet's untimely death is a tragedy.

03:09.890 --> 03:13.436
And I will not rest until
I find her killer, or killers.

03:13.561 --> 03:17.315
Oh, really, don't bother.
Nothing's going to bring our baby back.

03:17.315 --> 03:22.111
- No, I insist. I will make it my life's work...
- We're fine. Drop it.

03:24.613 --> 03:27.743
The next laser rock show
will begin in 20 minutes.

03:27.826 --> 03:31.705
You hear that, Brian? A laser rock show!
Come on, cheer up, would you?

03:31.705 --> 03:33.165
I don't feel like it.

03:34.834 --> 03:40.757
Binary code is a computer language in which
words are translated into zeroes and ones.

03:40.882 --> 03:43.052
Anything can be expressed in binary,

03:43.177 --> 03:46.305
as we demonstrate in this scene
from The Miracle Worker.

03:46.388 --> 03:49.724
0-1-1-0-1-0-0-1.

03:51.185 --> 03:54.106
0-1-1-0-1-0-0-1.

03:54.231 --> 03:57.150
0-1-1-0-1-0-0-1.

03:57.233 --> 04:00.278
01! 01!

04:05.703 --> 04:09.748
You don't think this is amazing?
When I saw this at the 1904 World's Fair,

04:09.873 --> 04:11.541
I nearly crapped my pants!

04:12.167 --> 04:14.127
All right! Virtual reality!

04:14.252 --> 04:16.839
Whoa! You guys gotta try this!

04:17.589 --> 04:20.302
Hey, look at me.
I'm a pole in a strip club! Oh!

04:20.302 --> 04:22.678
It's showtime.

04:22.803 --> 04:26.557
Oh! Oh, no! Oh, no! Oh!
Hey, stop! False alarm! Agh!

04:27.392 --> 04:30.729
Oh, my God! I'm flying. I'm flying!

04:31.980 --> 04:33.441
I'll have a Diet Sprite.

04:51.585 --> 04:54.087
You are a filthy whore.

04:59.093 --> 05:02.723
- OK, Johnny Depp or Richard Grieco?
- Oh, that's gross!

05:02.847 --> 05:04.934
- Yeah, let's not do this.
- Come on.

05:05.017 --> 05:08.896
If you're secure in your masculinity,
you can answer a hypothetical.

05:08.896 --> 05:12.233
Johnny Depp, cos he kind of
looks like a chick.

05:12.316 --> 05:16.613
- What about you, Peter?
- Oh, man. I don't know.

05:16.696 --> 05:20.784
Richard Grieco would probably appreciate
you more. Not take you for granted.

05:20.868 --> 05:23.913
With Johnny Depp,
he wouldn't really need you.

05:23.997 --> 05:26.623
He'd probably sneak out
after you fell asleep.

05:26.707 --> 05:31.003
Of course, with Johnny, you'd get
financial security. I'd go with Johnny.

05:31.087 --> 05:32.756
Oh, great.

05:35.384 --> 05:38.303
- Brian?
- Hey, Joe. How's it going?

05:38.387 --> 05:41.641
Good. You were doing
a little swerving back there.

05:41.641 --> 05:45.811
- Me and the boys were just...
- Whoa! You're off the meter, Brian.

05:45.895 --> 05:47.688
- You're under arrest.
- Come on.

05:47.688 --> 05:49.983
Move it!

05:50.066 --> 05:53.944
- One of you guys all right to drive?
- Yeah, I can do it.

05:55.823 --> 05:58.617
I'll meet you at The Drunken Clam.
We'll tie one on.

05:58.742 --> 06:01.952
I'm very disappointed in you.

06:07.293 --> 06:11.256
God, a DUl. I can't believe this.
I could actually go to jail.

06:11.338 --> 06:15.217
It's OK. You'll get through this DUl
and you'll be a better person for it.

06:15.301 --> 06:19.891
Hold on. Don't disguise his alcohol
dependence as a ticket to self-realisation.

06:20.016 --> 06:25.854
You're not one to talk. Remember when I gave
you apple juice and told you it was wine?

06:25.938 --> 06:30.653
- You are a special person.
- Thanks.

06:30.653 --> 06:35.659
Now, come on. I'm being serious.
I will be serious here for a second.

06:35.659 --> 06:37.952
Are you gonna listen to me?

06:38.035 --> 06:44.501
Are you gonna listen to me
so I can tell you that I respect you?

06:49.005 --> 06:51.508
Brian, I know this is a bad time for you.

06:51.592 --> 06:55.472
And if I have any advice to give you,
it is this: Grow a beard.

06:55.472 --> 06:58.475
I wish you'd shave that thing.
Beards are so ugly.

06:58.600 --> 07:00.978
- Hey!
- Oh, relax, Wooly Willy.

07:01.102 --> 07:03.396
There's lots of fun things you can do.

07:03.396 --> 07:05.357
- There we go.
- Thanks!

07:06.609 --> 07:10.279
On the charge of driving under
the influence, we find you guilty.

07:10.362 --> 07:12.990
Good call. Churn the butter.

07:12.990 --> 07:14.869
Ooh! Ooh!

07:14.952 --> 07:19.330
In lieu of jail time, I sentence you
to 100 hours of community service.

07:20.290 --> 07:21.751
Next item.

07:21.834 --> 07:25.713
Dearly beloved, we are gathered here
to join these two in holy matrimony.

07:25.797 --> 07:30.927
If anyone objects to this union,
speak now or for ever hold your peace.

07:31.010 --> 07:32.804
Quiet! You had your chance!

07:34.890 --> 07:40.187
- What are you doing for community service?
- I got assigned to Outreach to the Elderly.

07:40.313 --> 07:43.733
I gotta take care of an old woman
who hasn't been out in 30 years.

07:43.859 --> 07:46.778
When I got caught at school
with my hand down my pants,

07:46.861 --> 07:50.825
I had to keep it there for a whole week.
Ha! What a week!

07:50.950 --> 07:55.120
Taking care of this old woman'll be
like baby-sitting, with bigger diapers.

07:55.120 --> 07:57.832
Aha! So they do make bigger diapers!

07:57.915 --> 08:01.169
That deceitful woman told me
I'd have to use the toilet.

08:01.252 --> 08:04.381
Fie on the toilet! It's made slaves of you all.

08:04.506 --> 08:08.344
I've seen it sitting in there,
lazy, slothful porcelain layabout

08:08.469 --> 08:12.515
feeding on other people's doo-doos
while contributing nothing to society!

08:12.640 --> 08:14.182
You get a job!

08:17.730 --> 08:23.068
Pearl Burton? My name's Brian. I'm here
from the Outreach to the Elderly programme.

08:23.152 --> 08:25.237
You're late!

08:29.200 --> 08:31.619
- What the hell is this?
- Delousing powder!

08:31.703 --> 08:33.789
Everyone on the outside is filthy!

08:33.914 --> 08:38.083
- You could have warned me.
- OK. It's gonna burn like hell in 30 seconds.

08:38.167 --> 08:40.380
I like my tea at four, my dinner at six.

08:40.463 --> 08:43.298
I take my bath at seven
so I can listen to Paul Harvey.

08:43.298 --> 08:47.470
You'll warm up my bath with quick bursts
from the faucet during commercials.

08:47.553 --> 08:52.348
Paul Harvey moves seamlessly into
commercials. It's been 30 seconds.

09:00.191 --> 09:03.737
- Stop scratching that thing.
- I can't. It's itching like crazy.

09:03.737 --> 09:06.866
- Can I scratch your beard?
- You finished your homework?

09:06.949 --> 09:09.369
- Yes.
- OK then.

09:11.246 --> 09:14.583
Brian, you're quiet.
Is community service not going well?

09:14.665 --> 09:17.794
Lois, it's horrible.
I was cleaning her house all day.

09:17.920 --> 09:20.923
It's the worst job I've ever had.
Except for one.

09:22.299 --> 09:26.888
Excuse me. Would you like
to taste my smoked-meat log?

09:28.222 --> 09:32.519
- Here you go. Enjoy your food.
- Yes, enjoy your studio apartment.

09:33.981 --> 09:36.064
- You got something right here.
- Where?

09:36.148 --> 09:37.400
- Other side.
- Here?

09:37.525 --> 09:38.859
- The left side.
- Here?

09:38.984 --> 09:40.652
- Your other left.
- Where?

09:40.737 --> 09:42.322
- Up a little.
- Is it gone?

09:42.404 --> 09:43.781
- Go down.
- Is it gone?

09:46.994 --> 09:50.331
Is it gone? Agh!
Get it off! Get it off! Get it off!

09:50.456 --> 09:52.125
Peter, hold still!

09:52.125 --> 09:54.836
- Don't touch that bird!
- What's it to you?

09:54.836 --> 09:57.837
I'm Dr Goodman of the
Quahog Ornithological Society,

09:57.963 --> 10:01.177
ironically dining in a restaurant
that serves poultry.

10:01.301 --> 10:04.512
- Doctor, what is this?
- It's a very rare species.

10:04.637 --> 10:06.724
The endangered White-rumped Swallow.

10:06.724 --> 10:10.060
- Rump.
- This isn't funny, Chris!

10:10.143 --> 10:14.106
Swallow. Look,
just get rid of this bird, all right?

10:14.232 --> 10:19.739
I can't do that. Once the swallow has chosen
its nesting place, it's illegal to disturb it.

10:19.864 --> 10:22.031
He can't have a bird in his beard.

10:22.156 --> 10:27.455
You have to wait until the bird departs
of its own accord or you'll be prosecuted.

10:27.581 --> 10:29.749
Wow! You sure know a lot of stuff.

10:29.874 --> 10:32.585
- It's great to learn.
- Cos knowledge is power!

10:36.630 --> 10:39.342
- What is this? Spit soup?
- Tomato bisque.

10:40.385 --> 10:42.888
- What is this? Snot soup?
- Tomato bisque.

10:44.057 --> 10:48.019
- What is this? Diarrhoea soup?
- I'm not making you anything else. Eat it.

10:48.102 --> 10:51.647
Then I'll have to call the judge,
and that means you'll go to jail!

10:51.774 --> 10:56.654
You're one phone call away from getting
a human booster shot from a guy named Mali.

11:10.544 --> 11:11.794
- Dammit!
- Shh!

11:11.878 --> 11:14.506
Sorry! Sorry!

11:14.506 --> 11:17.636
- Shut up.
- There's nothing I can do.

11:17.719 --> 11:19.930
- Take it outside.
- Ever heard of a sitter?

11:20.014 --> 11:24.309
- It's an endangered species.
- I'll make you an endangered species!

11:24.392 --> 11:27.228
- Good comeback, Potsie!
- I'll kick your ass!

11:27.312 --> 11:29.398
- Yeah!
- Everybody shut up!

11:29.522 --> 11:32.442
He has stopped squawking.
He's receded into my beard.

11:32.526 --> 11:36.280
We can all watch the movie. Shut up.

11:36.405 --> 11:39.533
Eric, we're all going
to Marty's after the movie.

11:41.494 --> 11:45.458
- I love you so much.
- I love you too, honey.

11:45.583 --> 11:47.043
- Aah!
- Aah!

11:47.043 --> 11:48.294
- What's wrong?
- Aah!

11:48.377 --> 11:49.963
- Aah!
- Aah!

11:50.046 --> 11:54.341
That's it. You're history, pal. No bird
Frenches my wife and gets away with it.

11:56.429 --> 12:00.600
- Help! Help! I've broken my hip!
- Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

12:00.600 --> 12:01.851
Brian!

12:01.934 --> 12:07.065
- 5.3 seconds. I could have been dead by now!
- You're not really...?

12:07.149 --> 12:10.694
I heard you drop that light bulb, too.
That'll be 67 cents!

12:10.819 --> 12:15.198
- Go warm me up some diarrhoea soup!
- That's it! I've had it with you, you old hag!

12:15.198 --> 12:20.620
You're a miserable, dried-up shut-in, trying
to make everyone feel as bad as you do!

12:20.704 --> 12:24.584
Why don't you do the world
a big favour and drop dead?!

12:27.920 --> 12:30.840
- This last one won't open.
- You gotta jiggle it.

12:30.924 --> 12:32.717
- Like this?
- Let me get it.

12:32.801 --> 12:37.098
Oh, thanks. And... you know, drop dead.

12:39.392 --> 12:44.187
Get out of my beard,
you squawking bastard!

12:45.106 --> 12:47.942
Nothing. I was hoping
it wouldn't come to this.

12:47.942 --> 12:50.030
Oh, my God! Peter, no!

12:51.070 --> 12:53.784
Lois, the bird must die!

12:58.578 --> 13:01.498
It's gone! It's gone! Oh, thank God!

13:01.498 --> 13:03.586
Peter, what's that sound?

13:05.336 --> 13:07.755
Oh, my God. They're babies.

13:07.839 --> 13:11.176
Hey, look, Lois. There are
three of 'em, just like ours.

13:15.765 --> 13:18.268
And, uh... um...

13:19.644 --> 13:21.522
Sweet.

13:23.899 --> 13:26.526
We now return to
E's mysteries and scandals.

13:26.610 --> 13:29.322
- Pearl Burton, the Jingle Queen.
- Pearl?

13:29.447 --> 13:33.826
I'm AJ Benza. You won't find Pearl's name
on the Hollywood Walk of Fame.

13:33.826 --> 13:38.080
Yet from 1945 to 1960, you couldn't
turn on a radio or television

13:38.206 --> 13:41.126
without hearing one
of her trademark jingles.

13:41.210 --> 13:43.922
"You're only healthy when you're tan

13:44.047 --> 13:47.257
"So soak up all the sun you can

13:47.383 --> 13:51.137
"With Copper... Coppertone

13:51.220 --> 13:54.267
At her peak, Pearl Burton
earned 26 grand a year,

13:54.267 --> 13:58.229
which, by today's standards,
would be just under 49 billion dollars.

13:58.312 --> 14:03.108
- Brian, she's beautiful.
- Yeah, and that voice. I had no idea.

14:03.232 --> 14:07.405
In 1961, Pearl used an appearance
at Carnegie Hall to make the leap

14:07.405 --> 14:09.365
from jingle-singer to artist.

14:13.244 --> 14:17.916
That's "Habanera" from Carmen.
Oh, I've never heard it sung so beautifully.

14:18.041 --> 14:20.753
- Sing Coppertone!
- Yeah, Coppertone!

14:20.836 --> 14:23.965
- Do Doan's Pills!
- Sing Gold Bond Medicated Powder!

14:24.090 --> 14:26.176
- Pepsodent!
- Chiclets!

14:26.176 --> 14:30.556
No one has seen Pearl Burton since
that fateful night over 30 years ago.

14:30.639 --> 14:35.353
- She's presumed dead.
- My God. I said those awful things to her!

14:39.315 --> 14:41.401
Pearl!

14:46.699 --> 14:48.494
Pearl, don't do this!

14:48.575 --> 14:52.039
You should be happy.
I'm doing the world a big favour!

14:52.121 --> 14:54.415
Move! Your fur is making my feet sweat!

14:54.541 --> 14:57.127
Pearl, listen to me. I heard you sing.

14:57.252 --> 14:59.963
It was the most beautiful sound
I've ever heard.

15:00.047 --> 15:03.508
Oh, sure. Warbling for
Vick's VapoRub and Dippety-Do!

15:03.508 --> 15:04.635
No, I mean...

15:04.760 --> 15:08.097
Stop trying to talk me out of it!
I'm a pathetic sellout!

15:08.181 --> 15:10.808
No one who sings Carmen
like you is pathetic!

15:10.891 --> 15:13.727
- What?
- I heard you sing "Habanera".

15:13.811 --> 15:17.690
- You were sublime.
- You... you liked my aria?

15:17.773 --> 15:19.025
I was overwhelmed.

15:19.150 --> 15:23.822
You're the first person who ever
complimented my "Habanera". Thank you.

15:24.572 --> 15:29.036
Well... I'd better get going.
I'll see you tomorrow.

15:29.161 --> 15:32.790
- But you're not scheduled tomorrow.
- I know.

15:56.692 --> 16:01.573
And then the cow came out of the barn.
See? Look, there's the cow.

16:01.697 --> 16:03.449
And what does a cow say?

16:03.573 --> 16:07.829
Yes! Yes, that's right.
A cow says "Peep-peep-peep-peep. "

16:07.954 --> 16:10.874
- Peter, they're getting awfully big.
- So?

16:10.874 --> 16:14.502
A mother knows when it's time
for her babies to leave the nest.

16:14.627 --> 16:18.883
Hey, they're free to go
any time they want! Aah!

16:19.009 --> 16:20.760
Fine. I'll let 'em go.

16:31.313 --> 16:33.691
- Pearl, do you rent or own?
- Own what?

16:33.817 --> 16:39.447
Those wings, you angel.
That was fantastic. That was so incredible.

16:39.447 --> 16:44.118
What do you want for dinner? I was thinking
of making that lamb and rice you love.

16:44.243 --> 16:47.665
Pearl, what I'd really like
for dinner is to go out.

16:47.790 --> 16:52.796
Brian, you know I can't do that.
I haven't left this house in such a long time.

16:52.880 --> 16:55.715
- I'm afraid.
- I know. But I'll be with you.

16:55.797 --> 16:57.802
I don't know.

16:57.885 --> 17:01.137
There's so much you've missed
in the last 30 years.

17:01.137 --> 17:03.849
In fact, allow me to fill you in.

17:03.849 --> 17:06.978
"The '60s brought the hippie breed

17:07.061 --> 17:10.106
"And decades later
things have changed indeed

17:10.189 --> 17:13.652
"We lost the values but we kept the weed

17:13.735 --> 17:17.197
"You've got a lot to see

17:17.197 --> 17:20.409
"The Reagan years have laid the frame

17:20.534 --> 17:23.745
"For movie stars to play
the White House game

17:23.871 --> 17:26.875
"We're not too far
from voting Feldman-Haim

17:27.000 --> 17:30.002
"You've got a lot to see

17:30.128 --> 17:33.256
"The town of Vegas has got a different face

17:33.340 --> 17:36.466
"Cos it's a family place with lots to do

17:36.592 --> 17:41.682
"Where in the '50s, a man could mingle
with scores of all the seediest whores

17:41.807 --> 17:43.684
"Now his children can, too

17:43.684 --> 17:46.605
"You heard it from the canine's mouth

17:46.688 --> 17:49.816
"The country's changed -
that is, except the South

17:49.941 --> 17:52.736
"And you'll agree

17:52.862 --> 17:56.406
"No one really knows, my dear lady friend

17:56.490 --> 17:59.952
"Just quite how it all will end

18:00.035 --> 18:06.294
"So hurry cos you've got a lot to see

18:10.171 --> 18:13.384
"The baldness gene was cause for dread

18:13.509 --> 18:16.512
"But that's a fear that you can put to bed

18:16.637 --> 18:19.641
"They'll shave your ass
and glue it on your head

18:19.766 --> 18:23.311
"You've got a lot to see

18:23.395 --> 18:26.648
"The PC age has moved the bar

18:26.731 --> 18:29.986
"A word like "redneck" is a step too far

18:30.068 --> 18:33.115
"The proper term is "country music star"

18:33.198 --> 18:36.118
"You've got a lot to see

18:36.243 --> 18:39.579
"Our flashy cellphones
make people mumble "Gee whiz"

18:39.579 --> 18:42.709
"Look how important he is,
his life must rule. "

18:42.793 --> 18:46.045
"You'll get a tumour,
but on your surgery day

18:46.128 --> 18:50.842
"The doc will see it and say
"Wow, you must really be cool"

18:53.219 --> 18:56.348
- " Lots you may have missed
- " Like Pee Wee and his famous wrist

18:56.473 --> 18:59.684
"Or Sandy Duncan's creepy phony eye

18:59.810 --> 19:02.938
- " That Thundercats cartoon
- " Neil Armstrong on the moon

19:03.022 --> 19:06.483
"Neil Armstrong?
Wait, was he the trumpet guy?

19:09.487 --> 19:12.949
"So let's go see the USA

19:13.033 --> 19:18.998
"They'll treat you right unless
you're black or gay or Cherokee

19:19.082 --> 19:22.543
"But you can forgive
the world and its flaws

19:22.543 --> 19:25.964
"And follow me there because

19:26.089 --> 19:31.719
"You've still got a hell of a lot to see

19:32.763 --> 19:39.020
"You've got a lot to see

19:42.648 --> 19:48.405
Brian, I've missed so much! I wouldn't be
standing here right now if it wasn't for you!

19:52.160 --> 19:55.579
She's in here. Tell the disorderly
when you're ready to leave.

19:55.704 --> 19:58.708
- Don't you mean the orderly?
- No, I mean the disorderly.

19:58.834 --> 20:02.171
That's a doctor joke we like to make.
We also like Kevin Pollak.

20:03.422 --> 20:07.801
- Oh, my God, Pearl.
- Brian, I don't have much time.

20:07.885 --> 20:11.138
I never should have made you leave.
This is all my fault!

20:11.221 --> 20:13.932
Shh, shh, shh. Don't be so hard on yourself.

20:14.057 --> 20:18.313
Aside from the truck part,
this was the best day of my life.

20:18.439 --> 20:21.859
I only wish we could have
a little more time together.

20:21.984 --> 20:23.860
We can.

21:15.584 --> 21:17.044
Goodbye, kids.

21:28.181 --> 21:30.268
Goodbye, Pearl.

21:32.686 --> 21:34.773
Hey, who wants to see a dead body?

21:37.067 --> 21:40.194
- Rough week, huh?
- I've seen better.

21:40.194 --> 21:44.241
Brian, looks like somebody's
checking you out.

21:44.365 --> 21:48.203
Nah, I'm not ready yet.
Hey, you're getting some looks yourself.

21:52.500 --> 21:55.836
I'm not ready either.

21:55.837 --> 22:56.837
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru